# The REAL Way to Learn System Design

For every concept:

## Step 1 — Learn the Theory

Use:

* [ByteByteGo](https://bytebytego.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
* [System Design Primer GitHub](https://github.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
* [High Scalability](https://highscalability.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
* [Martin Kleppmann Book](https://dataintensive.net?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

But do NOT stay here too long.

Your goal:

* Understand:

  * Why it exists
  * What problem it solves
  * Tradeoffs
  * Failure scenarios

Example:

* Redis cache exists because DB becomes bottleneck
* Kafka exists because synchronous communication fails at scale

---

# Step 2 — Build It Yourself (MOST IMPORTANT)

This is where mastery happens.

For EVERY topic:

1. Create mini architecture
2. Run locally using Docker Compose
3. Stress test it
4. Break it intentionally
5. Observe behavior
6. Fix bottlenecks

